00:57:58,940 --> 00:58:01,540
and he wonders about his place in this country

1034
00:58:01,540 --> 00:58:04,420
and I would like to appreciate for passing that,

1035
00:58:04,420 --> 00:58:07,060
passing this resolution to honor immigrants.

1036
00:58:07,060 --> 00:58:09,580
And I understand that there was some tenetness

1037
00:58:09,580 --> 00:58:11,940
or some apprehension about passing this,

1038
00:58:11,940 --> 00:58:14,260
which I do not understand because I think it is only

1039
00:58:14,260 --> 00:58:15,460
full of goodwill and benign.

1040
00:58:15,460 --> 00:58:18,020
And I honestly think that it could go further.

1041
00:58:18,020 --> 00:58:20,740
I think that if you wanted to honor immigrants,

1042
00:58:20,740 --> 00:58:24,180
you should pass a formal resolution not to cooperate with ICE

1043
00:58:24,180 --> 00:58:27,500
should they become lawless in this county.

1044
00:58:30,500 --> 00:58:33,500
I don't think that it's that big of an ask.

1045
00:58:33,500 --> 00:58:34,340
Thank you.

1046
00:58:39,060 --> 00:58:40,300
That concludes our speakers

1047
00:58:40,300 --> 00:58:43,060
and we will go on to the rest of the meeting

1048
00:58:43,060 --> 00:58:45,140
and we will hear now from Mayor Battle.

1049
00:58:46,460 --> 00:58:47,820
Thank you, Madam President.

1050
00:58:47,820 --> 00:58:50,220
If I could ask Thomas Nunes,

1051
00:58:50,220 --> 00:58:54,060
Thomas, would you come up to the front, please?

1052
00:58:56,100 --> 00:58:59,100
Many of you know Mr. Nunes

1053
00:58:59,100 --> 00:59:02,100
