1058
00:59:24,860 --> 00:59:26,820
and he is our planning director.

1059
00:59:26,820 --> 00:59:29,060
And he does a marvelous job with planning the city

1060
00:59:29,060 --> 00:59:31,540
and does it on a day-to-day basis.

1061
00:59:31,540 --> 00:59:34,220
And Mr. Nunes, I would like to present you

1062
00:59:34,220 --> 00:59:35,780
with your 15-year pin.

1063
00:59:35,780 --> 00:59:38,260
I know you were wondering why you were up here,

1064
00:59:38,260 --> 00:59:40,380
but you've forgotten you have been here 15 years

1065
00:59:40,380 --> 00:59:41,420
and we want to say thank you.

1066
00:59:41,420 --> 00:59:43,180
Thank you for a great 15 years

1067
00:59:43,180 --> 00:59:45,140
and thank you for the job that you do every day.

1068
00:59:45,140 --> 00:59:46,140
Thank you, sir.

1069
00:59:46,140 --> 00:59:47,140
Yeah.

1070
00:59:47,140 --> 00:59:48,140
Yeah.

1071
00:59:48,140 --> 00:59:57,980
Now, Madam President, the only other thing

1072
00:59:57,980 --> 00:59:59,980
that I really wanted to mention today

1073
00:59:59,980 --> 01:00:02,220
is we have just finished

1074
01:00:02,220 --> 01:00:05,780
with Space and Missile Defense Conference Week.

1075
01:00:05,780 --> 01:00:10,220
We had 11,000 people in town, lots of people in town,

1076
01:00:10,260 --> 01:00:15,340
and it was a great symposium.

1077
01:00:16,740 --> 01:00:20,700
There was not a hotel room open in all of North Alabama,

1078
01:00:20,700 --> 01:00:24,140
we were very, very proud of the showing

1079
01:00:24,140 --> 01:00:25,340
that we were able to do.

1080
01:00:25,340 --> 01:00:29,340
Colonel Icke and Redstone Arsenal did a great job

1081
01:00:29,340 --> 01:00:30,940
of putting it together and making sure

1082
01:00:30,940 --> 01:00:34,140
that we could represent what Huntsville does,

1083
01:00:34,140 --> 01:00:35,420
which is a center of excellence.

1084
01:00:35,420 --> 01:00:37,140
I mean, we bring in the best and brightest,

1085
01:00:37,140 --> 01:00:39,300
and we become, and we do some things

1086
01:00:39,300 --> 01:00:41,220
that nobody else in the world does.

1087
01:00:41,220 --> 01:00:44,780
And you could see that at the symposium

1088
01:00:44,780 --> 01:00:47,140
over the last three days at the Civic Center.

1089
01:00:47,140 --> 01:00:49,420
If you tried to come park downtown,

1090
01:00:49,420 --> 01:00:51,420
you probably had a hard time finding a parking place

1091
01:00:51,420 --> 01:00:52,500
over the last three days,

1092
01:00:52,500 --> 01:00:56,900
but it was a great night for us, a great week for us,

1093
01:00:56,900 --> 01:01:01,900
and we are very excited to be looking forward to next year.

1094
01:01:02,180 --> 01:01:03,180
So thank you.

1095
01:01:04,420 --> 01:01:05,420
Thank you, Mayor.

1096
01:01:05,420 --> 01:01:06,420
Thank you, Mayor Battle.

1097
01:01:06,420 --> 01:01:07,580
We'll go on with Council Member Cummings

1098
01:01:07,620 --> 01:01:10,460
and we'll begin with Council Member John Merida.

1099
01:01:10,460 --> 01:01:11,700
Thank you.

1100
01:01:11,700 --> 01:01:14,980
I want to thank all those folks who came out

1101
01:01:14,980 --> 01:01:17,900
