1104
01:01:23,100 --> 01:01:26,180
and I look forward to bringing satisfactory resolution

1105
01:01:26,180 --> 01:01:28,900
to each of those issues that were mentioned.

1106
01:01:28,900 --> 01:01:32,540
I also wanna give a big heartfelt thank you to HPD,

1107
01:01:32,540 --> 01:01:37,000
the CROs for the North District Precinct, rather,

1108
01:01:37,000 --> 01:01:40,960
who were there, as well as their captain, Captain Widener,

1109
01:01:40,960 --> 01:01:43,400
who led a wonderful discussion on the value

1110
01:01:43,400 --> 01:01:46,880
of participating in the City's Community Watch Program

1111
01:01:46,880 --> 01:01:48,960
and all of the benefits that it brings

1112
01:01:48,960 --> 01:01:51,620
to the various communities that utilize it

1113
01:01:51,620 --> 01:01:55,300
to help keep down the levels of crime

1114
01:01:55,300 --> 01:01:58,520
and the cooperation between citizens

1115
01:01:58,520 --> 01:02:02,680
in any given neighborhood with the police department,

1116
01:02:02,680 --> 01:02:05,160
identifying the issues there,

1117
01:02:05,160 --> 01:02:10,160
and also one of the unsung benefits

1118
01:02:10,360 --> 01:02:13,360
of being in a Community Watch Program

1119
01:02:13,360 --> 01:02:18,360
is you are able to identify, or to identify to HPD

1120
01:02:19,980 --> 01:02:22,640
the good characters versus the bad characters

1121
01:02:22,640 --> 01:02:26,160
in any neighborhood so that the good characters

1122
01:02:26,160 --> 01:02:30,200
are not rounded up with the usual list of suspects.

1123
01:02:30,200 --> 01:02:32,720
So there are tremendous benefits

1124
01:02:32,720 --> 01:02:35,680
to being in a Community Watch Program

1125
01:02:35,680 --> 01:02:37,480
in individual neighborhoods.

1126
01:02:37,480 --> 01:02:41,200
If you are not part of a neighborhood that has a program,

1127
01:02:41,200 --> 01:02:45,680
please reach out to myself or some HPD officer,

1128
01:02:45,680 --> 01:02:47,840
and we'll be happy to give you information

1129
01:02:47,840 --> 01:02:51,320
of how your neighborhood can become a part of that network.

1130
01:02:51,320 --> 01:02:53,480
And that's it for me, Madam President.

1131
01:02:53,480 --> 01:02:54,440
Thank you, Mr. Meredith.

1132
01:02:54,440 --> 01:02:56,760
We'll now hear from Council Member Michelle Watkins.

1133
01:02:56,760 --> 01:02:57,760
Good evening.

1134
01:02:57,760 --> 01:02:59,320
I wanna thank House for Utilities

1135
01:02:59,320 --> 01:03:00,920
for coming out a couple of weeks ago.

1136
01:03:00,920 --> 01:03:04,080
They had a meeting to talk about the battery installation

1137
01:03:04,080 --> 01:03:05,400
in our community.

1138
01:03:05,400 --> 01:03:08,200
I wanna thank Wes Kelly and his staff.

1139
01:03:08,200 --> 01:03:10,760
I wanna thank Allison and Arts Huntsfield.

1140
01:03:10,760 --> 01:03:14,640
This past Friday, we had our quarterly art show

1141
01:03:14,640 --> 01:03:16,060
at Cary Hills.

1142
01:03:16,060 --> 01:03:20,200
We had a drum line and we had impromptu acts

1143
01:03:20,200 --> 01:03:24,280
