3040
02:27:22,980 --> 02:27:24,980
So I'm Tamar Ibarra.

3041
02:27:24,980 --> 02:27:30,980
I'm the operations manager at Notorious DOG Dog Rescue at 210 Stoke Street, Northwest.

3042
02:27:30,980 --> 02:27:32,980
Thank you.

3043
02:27:32,980 --> 02:27:38,980
We are a local 501C nonprofit dedicated to rescuing abused, abandoned, neglected, and discarded dogs.

3044
02:27:38,980 --> 02:27:44,980
We receive no government funding and everything we do is funded by donations and carried out by volunteers.

3045
02:27:44,980 --> 02:27:52,980
I'm here tonight because our rescue has become the default safety net for a growing animal welfare issue that requires a community response.

3046
02:27:52,980 --> 02:28:04,980
Over the past few years, we have seen an increasing number of dogs living in homeless encampments, particularly the area commonly known as tent city and the surrounding blocks, which is where we're also located.

3047
02:28:04,980 --> 02:28:07,980
This is not about judging people experiencing homelessness.

3048
02:28:07,980 --> 02:28:08,980
This is genuine.

3049
02:28:08,980 --> 02:28:11,980
Many genuinely care about their animals.

3050
02:28:11,980 --> 02:28:25,980
The problem is that we are repeatedly seeing dogs suffer because their owners are unable or sometimes unwilling to provide basic care, even after extensive assistance has been offered by us or Huntsville Animal Services.

3051
02:28:25,980 --> 02:28:37,980
Our rescue has provided food, veterinary care, vaccinations, transportation, collars, leashes, blankets, spay and neuter services, and even offered to accept animals into our rescue when owners can no longer care for them.

3052
02:28:37,980 --> 02:28:42,980
Unfortunately, our offers of spay and neuter services are almost always declined, allowing the cycle to continue.

3053
02:28:42,980 --> 02:28:49,980
What we are seeing over and over again are animals whose basic needs are not being met despite extensive assistance being offered.

3054
02:28:49,980 --> 02:28:57,980
From January of this year to July of this year, we've invested roughly seven thousand dollars in assistance.

3055
02:28:57,980 --> 02:29:02,980
That does not include medication, supplies, transportation, volunteer time or food.

3056
02:29:03,980 --> 02:29:09,980
This turns out to be an average of a minimum of a thousand dollars a month and twelve thousand dollars a year.

3057
02:29:09,980 --> 02:29:13,980
These cases we encounter are severe.

3058
02:29:13,980 --> 02:29:30,980
We have treated dogs suffering from pyometra requiring emergency surgery, rescued dogs with cords wrapped around their necks, responded to dog attacks and taken in puppies that tested positive for methamphetamine exposure after being found in environments where their owners were incapacitated by drug use.

3059
02:29:31,980 --> 02:29:39,980
These are not isolated incidents. They are reoccurring cases that consume limited nonprofit resources while animals continue to suffer.

3060
02:29:39,980 --> 02:29:46,980
I also want to acknowledge that Huntsville Animal Services has worked with us and that we appreciate the officers responding to the calls that we make.

3061
02:29:46,980 --> 02:29:51,980
However, our current system is not producing positive outcomes in many situations.

3062
02:29:51,980 --> 02:29:58,980
For example, dogs are routinely left tied to the fence outside of First Stop, which is nearby us, for hours.

3063
02:29:58,980 --> 02:30:02,980
Monday, August 3rd, one remained there for approximately three hours.

3064
02:30:02,980 --> 02:30:15,980
When these situations are reported, this particular day at 930 a.m. and 12 p.m. by me, the response is often that the dog has an owner and therefore little can be done.

3065
02:30:15,980 --> 02:30:21,980
That raises an important policy question. How is ownership being verified or defined?

3066
02:30:22,980 --> 02:30:29,980
Many of these dogs have no microchip, no vet records, establishing ownership, and they frequently change hands within the encampment.

3067
02:30:29,980 --> 02:30:36,980
If an ownership cannot be objectively verified and an animal is repeatedly found in conditions that threaten its welfare, there should be a clear...

3068
02:30:36,980 --> 02:30:40,980
Ms. Ebarra, I'm sorry, your time is up. Your three minutes is up.

