3077
02:31:18,980 --> 02:31:24,980
We'll hear next from Andrew Sullins. Following Mr. Sullins, we'll hear from Angelica Condry.

3078
02:31:24,980 --> 02:31:30,980
Good evening. My name is Andrew Sullins, and I'm a resident at 1410 Wells Avenue, right here in Huntsville.

3079
02:31:30,980 --> 02:31:31,980
Welcome.

3080
02:31:31,980 --> 02:31:38,980
I'm here today to express my concerns with the proliferation of flock automated license plate readers throughout the city of Huntsville.

3081
02:31:38,980 --> 02:31:51,980
These approximately 100 devices create point in time images of each passing vehicle, creating thousands of data points on tens of thousands of punts billions every day, accessible not only to local police but to law enforcement nationwide.

3082
02:31:51,980 --> 02:32:02,980
Flock and HPD fact sheets defend this technology by claiming images are merely single points in time, but thousands of data points easily assemble into a mosaic of our daily travel patterns.

3083
02:32:02,980 --> 02:32:06,980
These aggregated data points create a system prone to abuse.

3084
02:32:06,980 --> 02:32:11,980
Nearly every day we learn of yet another misuse, either nationally or right here in Alabama.

3085
02:32:11,980 --> 02:32:21,980
A journalistic investigation has found over 50 incidents in which officers have run thousands of checks on wives, girlfriends, mistresses and personal enemies.

3086
02:32:21,980 --> 02:32:29,980
In just the last month, officers in Moody and Springfield, Alabama were fired or forced to resign after conducting searches on their family members.

3087
02:32:29,980 --> 02:32:36,980
Flock proponents downplay these incidents as isolated and point to the mere ability to conduct audits as sufficient oversight.

3088
02:32:36,980 --> 02:32:44,980
They note that officers must enter a reason for each search, but neglect to mention that many log entries show big reasons such as test or investigation.

3089
02:32:44,980 --> 02:32:50,980
HPD says they continue to conduct system audits without any specifics or past findings.

3090
02:32:50,980 --> 02:33:00,980
Beyond the risk of abuse, there is also a clear disparity with more affluent, wider areas of south and east Huntsville having limited cameras along 231 and 431,

3091
02:33:00,980 --> 02:33:06,980
while working class communities of color in the north and west see dozens of devices deep into residential areas.

3092
02:33:06,980 --> 02:33:13,980
My previous commute from Aston Lake Road took me past three separate Flock hubs, while my new commute from Five Points takes me past Nudd.

3093
02:33:14,980 --> 02:33:19,980
If this is truly about safety, does the city not want to protect the people of southeast Huntsville?

3094
02:33:19,980 --> 02:33:26,980
Proponents point to solve crimes as justification, but we must ask ourselves if the ends justify the means.

3095
02:33:26,980 --> 02:33:31,980
If Huntsville stored all of our digital data, would we solve more crimes? Absolutely.

3096
02:33:31,980 --> 02:33:37,980
Would we, the people, happily accept the watchful eye of Bid Brother for this trade-off? Unlikely.

3097
02:33:37,980 --> 02:33:43,980
I urge the Council to adopt an ordinance banning the municipal use of these types of integrated devices in city limits.

3098
02:33:43,980 --> 02:33:56,980
If unwilling, I implore the Council to, at minimum, set a clear legal requirement for quarterly audits with at least a 20% random sample size and termination of any employee found to abuse the public trust placed in them.

3099
02:33:56,980 --> 02:33:59,980
I end with a quote from Benjamin Franklin.

3100
02:34:00,980 --> 02:34:07,980
Those who would give up essential liberty to purchase a little temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. Thank you.

3101
02:34:07,980 --> 02:34:08,980
Thank you, sir.

3102
02:34:08,980 --> 02:34:14,980
The next person to speak is Angelica Condry, who will be followed by Mariko Darling.

3103
02:34:14,980 --> 02:34:29,980
Good evening, Councilmembers. Huntsville 35811.

3104
02:34:29,980 --> 02:34:31,980
And your name, please, for the record.

3105
02:34:31,980 --> 02:34:32,980
Angelica Condry.

3106
02:34:32,980 --> 02:34:33,980
Thank you.

3107
02:34:33,980 --> 02:34:42,980
I'm here again tonight representing Rocket City Roller Derby, but I want to focus tonight on our appropriations application because I know we're coming up on budget season.

3108
02:34:42,980 --> 02:34:44,980
I know those numbers are on your mind right now.

3109
02:34:44,980 --> 02:34:54,980
We have submitted an appropriations request for $50,000, and obviously whatever amount the city is able to provide would be helpful, but I want you to know what that money would actually allow us to do.

3110
02:34:54,980 --> 02:35:00,980
We lost our long-term venue, which was affordable and sustainable for a small volunteer-run nonprofit.

3111
02:35:00,980 --> 02:35:03,980
Since losing it, we have been searching everywhere for a solution.

3112
02:35:03,980 --> 02:35:09,980
Parks and recreation has honestly been a life support for us this season, and we are incredibly grateful for that.

3113
02:35:10,980 --> 02:35:14,980
The basketball season is coming, and we know that we can't depend on those facilities indefinitely.

3114
02:35:14,980 --> 02:35:17,980
The $50,000 would help us actually get established somewhere.

3115
02:35:17,980 --> 02:35:29,980
It could help us pay the rent and the initial rent in a facility while we get it up and running, purchasing tables, chairs, and equipment we need to put down a proper track and make the space functional for our practices and events.

3116
02:35:29,980 --> 02:35:33,980
I'm also actively working on securing a warehouse that could potentially become that home.

3117
02:35:33,980 --> 02:35:38,980
If we're able to make that happen, this funding could help us turn an empty warehouse into a functional roller sports facility.

3118
02:35:38,980 --> 02:35:42,980
Eventually, depending on what we are able to secure, we could even look at something like a bank track.

3119
02:35:42,980 --> 02:35:48,980
We've talked to other skaters outside the area that have told me personally they would come to Huntsville specifically to skate if we had one.

3120
02:35:48,980 --> 02:35:50,980
This isn't just about roller derby, though.

3121
02:35:50,980 --> 02:35:55,980
We have roller hockey, figure skating, dance skating, speed skating, and other roller sports in this city.

3122
02:35:55,980 --> 02:35:59,980
There is a community here. It's just a community that doesn't currently have an appropriate facility.

3123
02:35:59,980 --> 02:36:02,980
Huntsville is already losing opportunities because of that.

3124
02:36:02,980 --> 02:36:09,980
This year we were supposed to host our annual fall mixer that is six teams worth of skaters coming from across the southeast and even the Midwest.

3125
02:36:09,980 --> 02:36:13,980
And it's not just skaters, it's coaches, officials, families, friends, and spectators.

3126
02:36:13,980 --> 02:36:18,980
All those people would have stayed in Huntsville hotels, eaten at Huntsville restaurants, shopped here, and spent money in our community.

3127
02:36:18,980 --> 02:36:22,980
Instead, because we couldn't secure an appropriate facility, this event is going to Nashville this year.

3128
02:36:22,980 --> 02:36:31,980
We also lost the opportunity to host the Yellow Hammer Roller Rumble, a two-day statewide tournament that would have brought four Alabama teams along with their supporters and spectators to Huntsville.

3129
02:36:31,980 --> 02:36:38,980
So these aren't hypothetical economic opportunities. These are two events that we are actually supposed to host, and we lost them because we don't have a facility.

3130
02:36:38,980 --> 02:36:42,980
When I first came to the city, I said we weren't asking you to simply hand us a building. I still believe that.

3131
02:36:42,980 --> 02:36:51,980
But the more I've worked with Parks and Rec and the more I've researched what's available, the more I believe Huntsville needs to start having a serious conversation about a multi-use roller sports facility.

3132
02:36:51,980 --> 02:36:56,980
The city has invested in Stoner Park. You've invested in Escape Park. You've invested in facilities for other growing sports.

3133
02:36:57,980 --> 02:37:04,980
I think roller sports deserves that same opportunity. So tonight I'm asking you to support our appropriations request to help us get on the path toward a sustainable home.

3134
02:37:04,980 --> 02:37:14,980
Because we aren't asking you to build something for one team, we are asking you to invest in a community that's already here, already growing, and that's already shown it can bring people and economic activity into Huntsville.

3135
02:37:14,980 --> 02:37:16,980
We just need somewhere to do it. Thank you.

3136
02:37:16,980 --> 02:37:18,980
Thank you.

3137
02:37:18,980 --> 02:37:23,980
The next person to speak will be Mariko Darling, who will be followed by Kyle Simpson.

3138
02:37:27,980 --> 02:37:31,980
Hello, my name is Mariko Darling. I live on Alpine Street in Huntsville, Alabama.

3139
02:37:31,980 --> 02:37:32,980
Welcome.

3140
02:37:32,980 --> 02:37:42,980
I also want to speak about roller derby with Rocket City Roller Derby. I want to say that we're grateful the city has continued to provide space for our practices and events.

3141
02:37:42,980 --> 02:37:47,980
However, the lack of advanced confirmation for gym use has become a serious obstacle.

3142
02:37:48,980 --> 02:37:59,980
When we don't know whether we are going to have a venue until close to the event date, we can't effectively advertise, sell tickets, coordinate with visiting teams, recruit volunteers, or build community support.

3143
02:37:59,980 --> 02:38:06,980
We understand that parks and recreation would ultimately like us to find a permanent home of our own, and we want that too.

3144
02:38:06,980 --> 02:38:12,980
But sustaining our own facility requires us to grow, and growth depends on successful, well promoted events.

3145
02:38:13,980 --> 02:38:20,980
Right now we're caught in a cycle where we're encouraged to become independent of the recreation centers,

3146
02:38:20,980 --> 02:38:26,980
while the uncertainty surrounding our current space makes it harder to build that support and resources necessary to do that.

3147
02:38:26,980 --> 02:38:36,980
This is becoming increasingly urgent as basketball season approaches, when once again we will face the possibility of losing both our practice and event space again.

3148
02:38:36,980 --> 02:38:40,980
We want roller derby to have a lasting place in Huntsville's recreation community.

3149
02:38:40,980 --> 02:38:45,980
We want to grow our events, bring people together, and eventually establish a home of our own.

3150
02:38:45,980 --> 02:38:48,980
But to get there, we need enough stability to build that future.

3151
02:38:48,980 --> 02:38:49,980
Thank you.

3152
02:38:49,980 --> 02:38:50,980
Thank you.

3153
02:38:50,980 --> 02:38:56,980
We'll now hear from Kyle Simpson, who will be followed by KMP Carroll.

3154
02:38:56,980 --> 02:39:07,980
My name is Kyle Simpson.

3155
02:39:07,980 --> 02:39:10,980
I live at 187 Heritage Brook Drive in Huntsville.

3156
02:39:10,980 --> 02:39:11,980
Thank you.

3157
02:39:11,980 --> 02:39:15,980
Good evening, Madam President, Mayor Battle, and members of the City Council.

3158
02:39:15,980 --> 02:39:23,980
I'm here to respectfully ask for your help restoring my access to the Huntsville Tennis Center, a public facility owned by the City of Huntsville.

3159
02:39:23,980 --> 02:39:31,980
I worked at the Tennis Center for about three years while I was in high school, and in 2023 I was terminated for not completing my closing duties properly.

3160
02:39:31,980 --> 02:39:33,980
I accepted that decision and moved on.

3161
02:39:33,980 --> 02:39:44,980
However, I have never been accused of any misconduct beyond that, and I was never told I was banned from the facility or prohibited from returning as a member of the public.

3162
02:39:44,980 --> 02:39:51,980
Shortly after my employment ended, I filed a complaint with the Alabama Department of Labor concerning my handling of alcohol while I was a minor.

3163
02:39:51,980 --> 02:39:56,980
I did so on the advice of my parents because I believed it was the appropriate way to address my concerns.

3164
02:39:56,980 --> 02:40:02,980
I took a break from tennis for about three years, and a few weeks ago I decided to start playing again.

3165
02:40:02,980 --> 02:40:08,980
For four consecutive weeks, I used the Tennis Center without any issues, and I even had my racket restrung there.

3166
02:40:08,980 --> 02:40:18,980
Then on July 29th, when I returned to pick up my racket, I was met at the front door by the managing director, Jock Simmons, who was also my former supervisor.

3167
02:40:19,980 --> 02:40:26,980
As I entered the facility, he told me verbatim, get out. You do not get to file complaints against us and play tennis here.

3168
02:40:26,980 --> 02:40:37,980
I left immediately. I did not argue or create a disturbance. I paid all my fees, and I have not caused any issues with the facility or its management.

3169
02:40:37,980 --> 02:40:44,980
To this day, I still have never received a written trespass notice, never been informed that I'm banned from the facility,

3170
02:40:44,980 --> 02:40:49,980
and never been told that I violated any rule as a patron of the Tennis Center.

3171
02:40:49,980 --> 02:40:54,980
I'm not asking the Council to punish anyone. I'm just asking for its fairness and clarity.

3172
02:40:54,980 --> 02:41:01,980
If there is an official policy that justifies excluding me from a public recreational facility, I would appreciate knowing what it is.

3173
02:41:01,980 --> 02:41:11,980
And if there isn't, I respectfully ask that my access to the Tennis Center be restored so that I can continue playing the sport I enjoy at a public facility that serves our community.

3174
02:41:11,980 --> 02:41:16,980
I would just like to say I've already taken this up with Parks and Rec, and they said it's outside of their scope.

3175
02:41:16,980 --> 02:41:22,980
I spoke with my city representative, and he recommended I come to this forum and take it up with you guys.

3176
02:41:22,980 --> 02:41:26,980
And I would just like to thank all of you for your time and consideration.

3177
02:41:26,980 --> 02:41:31,980
Thank you, sir. Thank you.

3178
02:41:31,980 --> 02:41:37,980
