3188
02:42:37,980 --> 02:42:43,980
I don't know, but I'm just trying to find out more about my city.

3189
02:42:43,980 --> 02:42:49,980
And this is the first time I'm doing so. And so I did. I want to find out what the rules are.

3190
02:42:49,980 --> 02:42:54,980
I can't bring up a motion or ask all questions.

3191
02:42:54,980 --> 02:42:58,980
So can anybody answer that question?

3192
02:42:58,980 --> 02:43:03,980
Ma'am, this is not a time for dialogue. If you'd like to meet with one of us afterwards, you're welcome to do so.

3193
02:43:03,980 --> 02:43:06,980
Okay. Thank you so much.

3194
02:43:06,980 --> 02:43:15,980
We'll now hear from Kayden Helbling, who will be followed by Victoria Kuzniastova.

3195
02:43:15,980 --> 02:43:18,980
Good evening. I'm Kayden Helbling, a Huntsville resident.

3196
02:43:18,980 --> 02:43:23,980
I'm the one who has been making the FLOC records requests. Other speakers have mentioned here in recent months.

3197
02:43:23,980 --> 02:43:30,980
Eight months ago, I asked the city for three administrative records from its FLOC license reader system.

3198
02:43:30,980 --> 02:43:36,980
The log of the searches run by city users, the log of outside agencies searching Huntsville's data and the data sharing settings.

3199
02:43:36,980 --> 02:43:41,980
I didn't ask for video, not case files, just the usage logs.

3200
02:43:41,980 --> 02:43:49,980
Records, the state's own LPR rules require to exist precisely so the public can tell whether a surveillance system is being used properly.

3201
02:43:49,980 --> 02:43:52,980
Over those eight months, the city changed its position four times.

3202
02:43:52,980 --> 02:44:01,980
First, a blanket denial, then an estimate of roughly $1 million, a number they reached by treating a single spreadsheet export as 1.7 million printed pages.

3203
02:44:01,980 --> 02:44:13,980
Then a claim that the electronic version of the files is impossible, even though FLOC's own published guide walks agents through downloading these exact logs as spreadsheets, a guide I sent them.

3204
02:44:13,980 --> 02:44:16,980
And then on August 3rd, I received a final denial.

3205
02:44:16,980 --> 02:44:21,980
The city now says there is no difference between the oversight logs and the license plate data itself.

3206
02:44:21,980 --> 02:44:25,980
And that even though it can produce these files electronically, it doesn't have to.

3207
02:44:25,980 --> 02:44:28,980
My only remaining option, they told me, is court.

3208
02:44:28,980 --> 02:44:40,980
Meanwhile, Blount County, Alabama, has the same Open Records Act, same records, and it gave a complete FLOC audit log to a newspaper this summer as one spreadsheet in about two months.

3209
02:44:40,980 --> 02:44:44,980
The same thing that Huntsville says would cost me a million dollars.

3210
02:44:44,980 --> 02:44:47,980
That Blount County log also showed exactly why these records matter.

3211
02:44:47,980 --> 02:44:58,980
96% of the searches had no case number attached, and nearby in St. Clair County audit logs are how one officer was terminated and another resigned this summer over unauthorized searches.

3212
02:44:58,980 --> 02:45:02,980
In one case, searches of the officer's own family.

3213
02:45:02,980 --> 02:45:05,980
These logs are not anti-police.

3214
02:45:05,980 --> 02:45:07,980
They are how misuse gets caught.

3215
02:45:07,980 --> 02:45:12,980
The CGS standards the city brought up in my meeting with them require this logging for exactly that reason.

3216
02:45:12,980 --> 02:45:18,980
Every FLOC item this council has passed went through unanimously, mostly on consent without discussion.

3217
02:45:18,980 --> 02:45:21,980
Those contracts auto-renew unless someone acts.

3218
02:45:21,980 --> 02:45:26,980
I believe one window is as soon as this fall, and the master agreement comes up in January.

3219
02:45:26,980 --> 02:45:28,980
And the council doesn't have to wait.

3220
02:45:28,980 --> 02:45:32,980
The MOU allows termination for convenience on 90 days notice.

3221
02:45:32,980 --> 02:45:41,980
A couple weeks ago, Council President Robinson suggested the city share its usage data more broadly, and Councilman Meredith announced a town hall on FLOC.

3222
02:45:41,980 --> 02:45:42,980
I welcome both.

3223
02:45:42,980 --> 02:45:44,980
And I ask a simple.

3224
02:45:44,980 --> 02:45:55,980
Before anything renews, put the system on a public agenda with the actual usage data in front of you, and make your decision and keeping it on and keeping it an on the record decision, not a default.

3225
02:45:55,980 --> 02:45:56,980
Thank you.

3226
02:45:56,980 --> 02:45:57,980
Thank you.

